-- title:
--   Level automorphisms preserve the j-chart algebra and fix y
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime and $M'$ a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $q\ell$, let $\zeta \in L$ be a primitive $q$-th root of unity, $\xi \in L$ a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity, and assume $\zeta = \xi^{\ell}$. Let $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ be the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), the kernel of reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, with the kernel of reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^\times$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subset L((t))$ obtained as the $L$-subfield generated by the image, under coefficientwise extension of scalars $\mathbb{Q} \to L$ on Laurent series, of the function field of $X_{H_1}(q^2M')$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with $\mathrm{Frac}(A) = L$, with $q$ in its maximal ideal and with $\zeta$ in the image of $A \to L$, made an $A$-algebra base for $K$ compatibly with $L$; let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion the coefficient image of $j_q = t^{-1}\cdot(\text{power series } j_{\mathrm{Num}})$, and write $\mathcal{A}_{\mathrm{fin}}$ for `chartAlgFin`, the $A$-subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$. Let $z$ be a point of the two-chart integral model $X = \mathrm{Spec}\,\mathcal{A}_{\mathrm{fin}} \sqcup_{\,\cdot\,} \mathrm{Spec}\,\mathcal{A}_{\infty}$ of $(A,K,j)$ such that the germ at $z$ of the image of $\varpi$ under the structural morphism $X \to \mathrm{Spec}\,A$ on global sections lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk at $z$, and let $y$ be a point of $\mathrm{Spec}\,\mathcal{A}_{\mathrm{fin}}$ mapping to $z$, assumed supersingular in the sense that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : \mathcal{A}_{\mathrm{fin}} \to \Omega$ with kernel the prime of $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7) $\Omega$, i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero point killed by $q$. The conclusion is a conjunction. First: for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and every $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ satisfying `IsLevelAutAt` for the data $(L,q,\zeta,q,q^2M',H_1,\gamma^{-1},K)$ — that is, for all weights $k$, all modular forms $f,g$ of weight $k$ on the group attached to $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansions and $g$ having nonzero associated series, all $x \in K$ whose Laurent expansion is the coefficient image of the ratio of those series, and every embedding $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota\zeta = e^{2\pi i/q}$, one has $\iota_*(\tau x)\cdot \mathrm{qExp}(g\mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\, q\, \gamma^{-1}) = \mathrm{qExp}(f\mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\, q\, \gamma^{-1})$ — the automorphism $\tau$ maps $\mathcal{A}_{\mathrm{fin}}$ into $\mathcal{A}_{\mathrm{fin}}$. Second: if in addition $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod{\ell}$, then for such a $\tau$, given a proof that $\tau$ preserves $\mathcal{A}_{\mathrm{fin}}$, the induced endomorphism of $\mathcal{A}_{\mathrm{fin}}$ satisfies $\tau(a) - a \in y$ for every $a \in \mathcal{A}_{\mathrm{fin}}$.
--
--   This packages the two witness-free equivariance properties of the level automorphisms of the base-changed function field of $X_{H_1}(q^2M')$ at a supersingular point of the $j$-finite chart: stability of the chart algebra, and triviality of the action on the residue field at $y$ for $\gamma$ congruent to a lower triangular unipotent matrix modulo $\ell$. It is the $\Gamma_1(\ell)$-frame variant, valid with no lower bound on $q$, and feeds the computations of the stalks of the Drinfeld chart and the inertia action used in the construction of the full-level model.
